I.K.E. Windows engine: allow the proprietary formats with FFmpeg's free codecs

Upstream refuses proprietary_codecs=true together with
ffmpeg_branding="Chromium". On Windows that is exactly the build I.K.E.
wants: the formats are known, FFmpeg decodes none of the patented ones,
Windows does. (Vivaldi relaxes the same assert for its own build.)

Licence: BSD-3-Clause, as the Chromium file it changes.

diff --git a/chromium/media/BUILD.gn b/chromium/media/BUILD.gn
index 10c65d1d..b208d471 100644
--- a/chromium/media/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chromium/media/BUILD.gn
@@ -91,7 +91,10 @@ buildflag_header("media_buildflags") {
   }
 }
 
-if (proprietary_codecs && media_use_ffmpeg) {
+# I.K.E.: on Windows the engine is built with the proprietary formats known
+# (MP4, H.264, AAC) and FFmpeg limited to its free codecs; H.264 and AAC are
+# decoded by Windows (Media Foundation). So this combination is wanted there.
+if (proprietary_codecs && media_use_ffmpeg && !is_win) {
   assert(
       ffmpeg_branding != "Chromium",
       "proprietary codecs and ffmpeg_branding set to Chromium are incompatible")
